>> title: Chicken Tikka
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, indian, yogurt, grill, starter
>> counters: Curry House, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: murgh tikka, tikka, chicken tikka kebab, tandoori chicken tikka
>> pairs-with: tandoori-marinade, mint-chutney, kachumber
>> servings: 6
>> time: 7 hr
>> slack: narrow — a domestic grill gets half a tandoor's heat and takes twice as long, so the fourteen minutes is a race between the crust setting and the thigh drying out; six hours in the marinade or eight makes no difference, and the whole dish is decided at the fire
>> step.1: slash and marinate 6 hr
>> step.2: thread on skewers, alternating
>> step.3: grill 14 min, turning, until the edges blacken
>> step.4: brush and dust, off the heat

Marinate @boneless chicken thighs{2%lb}(900 g; cut in 2-in pieces and slashed to the middle) in @tandoori marinade{1 1/2%cup}(360 g; the marinade recipe) ~marinate{6%hr}, covered, in the fridge.

Thread @&(~1)marinated chicken{} onto metal #skewers{} with @red onion{1}(cut in 1-in squares, layers separated) and @green bell pepper{1}(in 1-in squares), leaving a finger's gap between the pieces so the heat gets all the way round.

Grill @&(~1)skewers{} over the hottest charcoal you can build, or under a #broiler{} on the top rung, ~grill{14%min}, turning every few minutes, until the marinade has set into a dry crust and the high edges have gone properly black.

Brush @melted ghee{2%Tbs}(28 g) over @&(~1)cooked tikka{} and dust it with @chaat masala{1/2%tsp} and @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) off the heat.

This is what goes on the skewer the tandoori marinade was written for, and until now nothing did. A tandoor runs at about 480°C against a clay wall, which cooks a piece of thigh through in six minutes and chars it before it can dry out; a domestic grill or broiler gets perhaps half that and takes twice as long, so this is honestly a different dish and the way to keep it close is thigh rather than breast, and heat rather than patience. The same skewers, chopped off and dropped into a makhani gravy, are butter chicken.
